Project Overview :-

This project is an embedded safety system designed to detect harmful gas leakage (LPG/Butane) and abnormal temperature levels in real time. It uses an Arduino-based microcontroller system integrated with MQ gas sensor and LM35 temperature sensor to monitor environmental conditions and trigger alerts.

The complete hardware design is developed in KiCad, including schematic and PCB layout for a compact and professional embedded solution.

Working Principle:-
The MQ gas sensor (MQ-6/MQ-2) detects LPG/gas concentration in the air.
The LM35 temperature sensor measures ambient temperature.
Arduino reads both analog signals.
If thresholds are exceeded:
🔴 Buzzer activates for gas leakage
🔵 LED turns ON for high temperature alert'


Key Features:-
Real-time gas leakage detection
Temperature monitoring system
Dual alert system (LED + Buzzer)
Compact PCB design using KiCad
Arduino-based simple embedded logic
Low-cost and scalable safety solution

